    "opening": "A retail store reaches operating break-even when the contribution from its sales covers the shop's monthly expenses. In the example below, a $40 average receipt leaves $19.80 after stock, sale-related costs and fees; the shop needs 354 receipts to cover $4,200 of overhead and $2,800 of owner pay.",
